{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>באדם</b> (in a person). Here and the other: או באדם אשר יטמא לו (or concerning a person who becomes impure through him). And בוגדים באדם תוסיף (traitors increase against a person) — אשר שלט האדם באדם (that a person rules over a person). בוגדים באדם תוסיף refers to the strange woman who seduces a person until he obeys her, and this is אשר שלט האדם באדם — she rules over him; and if he obeys her, in the end he is stricken with tzara'at and becomes impure like a corpse.\n\nNegaim is juxtaposed to the woman who gives birth, to teach that whoever does not observe the laws of niddah — his children become metzoraim. (Another interpretation:) HaShem says to the one who gives birth: if you improve your deeds, see what I created above you — cattle and beast for your food; and if you spoil your deeds, negaim are at your side."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The comment begins with a masoretic observation about the phrase באדם appearing in this verse and elsewhere, then cites two juxtaposition-readings from Proverbs 16:17 (בוגדים באדם תוסיף) and Ecclesiastes 8:9 (אשר שלט האדם באדם) which are linked thematically to the strange woman motif; the second paragraph shifts to the juxtaposition of parashat negaim after parashat yoledet."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:23.510744157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}